15: def main(input_grid):
16:     """
17:     March each opposite-side pixel pair toward the center and mark the meeting point gray.
18: 
19:     Input structure:
20:     - Non-black single pixels appear in pairs on opposite sides of a black grid.
21:     - Each pair lies on a shared row or column after considering horizontal or vertical reflection.
22:     - Distances are arranged so each pair has one meeting cell.
23: 
24:     Rule:
25:     - Detect each single-pixel component.
26:     - Match it to the one non-background reflected pixel on the opposite side.
27:     - Move both endpoints toward each other, leaving trails of their own colors and coloring the meeting cell gray.
28: 
29:     Key insight:
30:     - Opposite-side reflection identifies the pairings, and simultaneous inward motion creates the two-color trails.
31:     """
32:     # Plan:
33:     # 1. Detect the pixels
34:     # 2. Associate each pixel with its matching pair
35:     # 3. Make them attract/march toward each other until they meet in the middle, leaving a trail of their own color
